>> title: Turkey Brine
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: thanksgiving, turkey, brine, poultry, make-ahead
>> counters: Meat and Three, Smokehouse
>> pairs-with: turkey-pan-gravy, cranberry-sauce
>> servings: 12
>> time: 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the brine is poured over ice and held below 40°F for the whole eight to twelve hours, and a bird brining warm is a food-safety failure rather than a seasoning mistake; past twelve hours the breast also goes spongy and salty, and neither undoes
>> step.1: simmer, stir until dissolved
>> step.2: steep off the heat 20 min
>> step.3: stir in
>> step.4: pour over ice, chill below 40°F, brine 8 to 12 hr

Bring @water{1%gal}(4 L) to a simmer in a large #stockpot{} with @kosher salt{2%cups}(285 g; Diamond Crystal, or 1 1/4 cups Morton) and @dark brown sugar{1%cup}(215 g), stirring until they dissolve.

Add @black peppercorns{2%Tbs}(cracked), @allspice berries{1%Tbs}, @bay leaves{6}, @fresh thyme{6%sprigs}, and @garlic{1%head}(halved crosswise) to @&(~1)salted water{}, take it off the heat, and steep ~{20%min}.

Stir @orange{1}(quartered) and @yellow onion{1}(quartered) into @&(~1)brine{}.

Pour @&(~1)hot brine{} over @ice water{1%gal}(4 L) and chill it below 40°F (4°C) before a 12 to 16 lb turkey goes in for 8 to 12 hours.
